# The headroom guard for the skill-5 crash (the `jets` flight: a jet's missile, the chopper lost
# among explosions, CHOPPER DOWN typing over them). Every picture of it is blitter-bound and the
# worst ones were 97% on the A500 (limit 97: layout sensitive, it flipped to 98 with a dropped
# frame four times on unrelated code). Real savings (merged erases of a crowd, a typing plan for
# the lost chopper's lines, a cover walk that stops at the last person, a HUD scan that stops
# at the first letter it cannot afford) took it to 92; this holds the line at 94, with the
# typed text itself checked: three shots of it, recorded from the build before those savings, so
# the saved work shows no difference in any pixel.
start-at boarding
key 0x63
key 0x28
wait 5
key 0x05
wait 30
expect-serial "difficulty=5"
press up 40
wait-serial "jet tell"
wait-serial "jet fire"
wait-serial "chopper lost" 1200
# (the lines start typing 40 pictures after the crash, two letters a picture)
wait 44
screenshot first
wait 8
screenshot second
wait 90
screenshot typed
expect-no-serial "AGK ERR"
expect-no-dropped-frames
expect-max-load 94
